# <%= @module %>

<!-- After the name, the thesis in a few words, as "<%= @module %>: <what it makes possible>". Then
a scenario in a blockquote: one person, one day, what this application lets them do that they
could not do before. Then two or three paragraphs: what it does, and why that matters. -->

<%= @section %>
## The process it owns

<!-- The business process this application owns, and who owns it: the person who approves its
contracts. What starts a run of it, and what ends one. -->

## Who it is for

<!-- The people who use it, each with the job they do through it and what tells them it worked. -->

## Principles

<!-- Numbered, each one sentence and then why. A principle settles a design question: when two
choices are both correct, the principle says which one this application makes. They may narrow
EHOS's principles above, never contradict them. -->

## What it will not do

<!-- What it deliberately leaves out, including what belongs to another application. -->

## Where it is heading

<!-- What comes next, and what is still open. -->
